{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1573834710,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDMwOTg5OTMzMw=="},"target":"4c93aa78a8b1787b6860eb5c2294434dd74e24c9603ef3e96777ceafab721bc3","message":"Demo dataset with 100k tiny files. A size like this is often considered the upper sensible limit of numbers of files.  Each file is placed in a 4th-level subdirectory, because I find that is a frequent average depth in the datasets that I work with.\n\n```sh\n$ for i in $(seq 100000); do s=$(uuid | tr '-' '/'); mkdir -p ${s:5:19} \u0026\u0026 echo $s \u003e ${s:5}; done\n# [7min, total size \u003c4MB]\n```\n\nCreate a dataset\n\n```sh\n/tmp/big % time datalad create -f\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/big \ncreate(ok): /tmp/big (dataset)                                                               \ndatalad create -f  1.03s user 0.52s system 66% cpu 2.327 total\n```\n\n```sh\n/tmp/big (git)-[master] % time datalad save\nTotal (100000 ok out of 100000): 100%|██████████████████| 3.70M/3.70M [12:50\u003c00:00, 12.0kB/s]\n\u003csnip 99999 lines\u003e\nadd(ok): ffe/07be/11ea/ba1c/1fdd75885bdc (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 100000)\n  save (ok: 1)\ndatalad save  781.46s user 189.75s system 109% cpu 14:46.91 total\n```\n\nFirst, it works! Second, every ~30k files, my machine took a break (desktop sluggish). It seems inside `git-annex-add` numerous `git ls-files` processes (among others) are started. I am attaching a `pstree` of a moment in such a phase that has ~100 such processes running.\n\n[ptree.txt](https://github.com/datalad/datalad/files/3852232/ptree.txt)\n\nNB: while we are calling `git-annex-add` in batches with long lists of filenames already, `git-annex` itself further splits to-be-processed files into (smaller) batches.\n\nThe result renderer output is completely useless (100k `add(ok)` lines), nobody knows if there was an important message on top.\n\nIt took 2x longer to save the files than to create them on the file system -- not too bad IMHO.\n\n```sh\n% time datalad status\ndatalad status  60.22s user 13.44s system 61% cpu 2:00.10 total\n% time datalad status -t raw\ndatalad status -t raw  6.09s user 1.45s system 100% cpu 7.487 total\n\n% time datalad save\ndatalad save  8.90s user 1.56s system 99% cpu 10.485 total\n```\n\nSensible IMHO. With a hot cache `git status` does\n\n```\n% time git status\nOn branch master\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\ngit status  0.42s user 0.94s system 127% cpu 1.064 total\n```\n\nand here some truths:\n\n```\n/tmp/big (git)-[master] % find . |wc -l\n506736\n/tmp/big (git)-[master] % find .git |wc -l\n296571\n /tmp/big (git)-[master] % du -sh .git\n1.3G    .git\n/tmp/big (git)-[master] % git gc --aggressive\nEnumerating objects: 425779, done.\nCounting objects: 100% (425779/425779), done.\nDelta compression using up to 4 threads\nCompressing objects: 100% (321825/321825), done.\nWriting objects: 100% (425779/425779), done.\nTotal 425779 (delta 11506), reused 414271 (delta 0)\ngit gc --aggressive  36.98s user 0.80s system 294% cpu 12.810 total\n/tmp/big (git)-[master] % du -sh .git\n1.3G    .git\n/tmp/big (git)-[master] % du -sh .git/annex\n1.2G    .git/annex\n/tmp/big (git)-[master] % du -sh .git/annex/objects\n1.2G    .git/annex/objects\n/tmp/big (git)-[master] % du -hc *\n\u003csnip\u003e\n821M    total\n```\n\nI did another test run with 500k files, but my machine ooops'ed after almost exactly one hour.It started to throw `add(error)` results afterwards.On reboot it took 8min to empty `/tmp` ;-)","files":null},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1573833863,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MjgwMzE2MDIzNQ=="},"title":"Behavior with large N datasets","was":"Behavior with large N datasets"},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1573834727,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhY