t grows\n          7.3M    db\n          17M     db-shm\n          7.5G    db-wal\n4.5K    .git/annex/keys.cache\n512     .git/annex/keys.lck\n3.6G    .git/annex/objects\n1.0K    .git/annex/othertmp\n512     .git/annex/othertmp.lck\n512     .git/annex/precommit.lck\n512     .git/annex/sentinal\n4.5K    .git/annex/sentinal.cache\n512     .git/annex/smudge.lck\n```\n\nI will report once it finishes, but @joeyh do you already see an obvious issue here? The file system load (ZFS) is essentially zero, but the git-annex process is going full tilt on CPU.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1574372102,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU1NzI4MjM0MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3869#issuecomment-557282341"},"message":"This probably has to do with sqlite's performance with a million or so\nINSERTs (with index updates) and probably twice as many SELECTs.\n\n\u003e 7.5G    .git/annex/keys\n\nThe size of that database seems suspicious to me. I see a linear growth\nin the database size while unlocking files, of approx 1kb per file\n(of course long filenames would make it larger). So with half a million\nfiles the database size should be around half a gigabyte. Tested only up\nto 15000 files, perhaps sqlite needs more at scale.\n\nOf course, unlock also has to copy every annexed object to the work tree\nfile, so will double the size of the repo at least (maybe more if there\nare duplicates). Setting annex.thin will help with that.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1574373968,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU1NzI5Mzk4OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3869#issuecomment-557293988"},"message":"unlock definitely gets slower as the total number of files increases:\n\njoey@darkstar:/tmp/bigdb2\u003efor n in $(seq 1 500); do for x in $(seq 1 1000); do echo $n-$x\u003e$n-$x;done; git annex joey@darkstar:/tmp/bigdb2\u003efor n in $(seq 1 500); do for x in $(seq 1 1000); do echo $n-$x\u003e$n-$x;done; git annex add --quiet; git annex unlock --quiet; echo \"pass $n\"; ls -l .git/annex/keys/db; done | ts -i\n00:00:20 pass 1\n00:00:00 -rw-r--r-- 1 joey joey 860160 Nov 21 17:42 .git/annex/keys/db\n00:00:57 pass 2\n00:00:00 -rw-r--r-- 1 joey joey 1699840 Nov 21 17:43 .git/annex/keys/db\n00:02:03 pass 3\n00:00:00 -rw-r--r-- 1 joey joey 2527232 Nov 21 17:45 .git/annex/keys/db\n00:01:51 pass 4\n00:00:00 -rw-r--r-- 1 joey joey 3383296 Nov 21 17:47 .git/annex/keys/db\n00:02:26 pass 5\n00:00:00 -rw-r--r-- 1 joey joey 4186112 Nov 21 17:49 .git/annex/keys/db\n\nDoesn't look exponential, at least with those relatively few 5k files...\n\nI do wonder if the significantly larger than expected db size in\nMichael's case indicates something beyond that.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1574403481,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU1NzQwNjE4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3869#issuecomment-557406183"},"message":"Thx @joeyh for the initial sanity check. The `unlock` process eventually finished after 16h. Other than the time, the state of the repo looks good:\n\n```\n~/big/.git/annex (git)-[master] % du -shc *\n512     gitqueue.lck\n27M     index\n4.5K    index.lck\n4.1M    journal\n512     journal.lck\n119M    keys\n4.5K    keys.cache\n512     keys.lck\n3.6G    objects\n512     othertmp.lck\n512     precommit.lck\n512     sentinal\n4.5K    sentinal.cache\n512     smudge.lck\n3.7G    total\n\n~/big (git)-[master] % du -sh\n6.3G    .\n1.7G    .git/objects\n\n[after `git gc --aggressive`]\n~/big (git)-[master] % du -sh\n5.0G    .\n243M    .git/objects\n```\n\nI have now started an initial `git status`\n```\n% git status\nRefresh index: 0% (127/539528)\n```\nIt does about two objects per second, so if the speed is maintained, it will run for 74 days. It is crunching through the smudge filters\n\n```\nmih@data1 ~ % pstree -p 162314 -la\ngit,162314 status\n  ├─sh,33561 -c git-annex smudge --clean -- '01a/061e/11ea/950e/078d4d322ab0' git-annex smudge --clean -- '01a/061e/11ea/950e/078d4d322ab0'\n  │   └─git-annex,33562 --library-path /usr/lib/git-annex.linux//usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/gconv:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/audit:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//etc/ld.so.conf.d:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//lib64:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//lib/x86_64-linux-gnu: /usr/lib/git-annex.linux/shimmed/git-annex/git-annex smudge --clean -- 01a/061e/11ea/950e/078d4d322ab0\n  │       ├─git,33582 --library-path /usr/lib/git-annex.linux//usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/gconv:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/audit:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//etc/ld.so.conf.d:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//lib64:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//lib/x86_64-linux-gnu: /usr/lib/git-annex.linux/shimmed/git/git --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. --literal-pathspecs cat-file --batch\n  │       ├─git,33583 --library-path /usr/lib/git-annex.linux//usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/gconv:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/audit:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//etc/ld.so.conf.d:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//lib64:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//lib/x86_64-linux-gnu: /usr/lib/git-annex.linux/shimmed/git/git --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. --literal-pathspecs cat-file --batch-check=%(objectname) %(objecttype) %(objectsize)\n  │       ├─git,33584 --library-path /usr/lib/git-annex.linux//usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/gconv:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/audit:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//etc/ld.so.conf.d:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//lib64:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu:/usr/lib/git-annex.linux//lib/x86_64-linux-gnu: /usr/lib/git-annex.linux/shimmed/git/git --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. --literal-pathspecs check-attr -z --stdin annex.backend annex.numcopies annex.largefiles --\n  │       ├─{git-annex},33577\n  │       ├─{git-annex},33578\n  │       ├─{git-annex},33579\n  │       └─{git-annex},33581\n  └─{git},33560\n```\n\nCPU load is negligible (~10%) , and the file system (ZFS on NVMe) is essentially idle. Do we see the cost of creating processes? But even then, two objects per second don't seem realistic.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1574439883,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU1NzU5ODM5MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3869#issuecomment-557598390"},"message":"Michael Hanke wrote:\n\u003e Thx @joeyh for the initial sanity check. The unlock process eventually finished\n\u003e after 16h. Other than the time, the state of the repo looks good:\n\u003e \n\u003e 119M    keys\n\nNow I really wonder what was in the database when it was 7 gb in size,\nmust have been a lot of tmp files..\n\nIf I got the numbers right, it unlocked 10 files/second; I'd be curious\nhow fast unlock of 1000 files in a small repo runs there, to get a baseline\nto compare with and see how it degrades at scale.\n\n\u003e I have now started an initial git status\n\u003e \n\u003e % git status\n\u003e Refresh index: 0% (127/539528)\n\u003e \n\u003e It does about two objects per second, so if the speed is maintained, it will\n\u003e run for 74 days. It is crunching through the smudge filters\n\u003e \n\u003e CPU load is negligible (~10%) , and the file system (ZFS on NVMe) is\n\u003e essentially idle. Do we see the cost of creating processes? But even then, two\n\u003e objects per second don't seem realistic.\n\nI saw in your ps that you're using the standalone git-annex build, so it\nhas to bootstrap itself with a shell script, find the libraries etc,\nevery time. That dominates the startup time. If that used a static C\nshim, it would be faster, but faster yet is a na